From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:26:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] liblog: abort message when built for Android

logger_write.cpp calls android_set_abort_message from the default
aborter under __ANDROID__, but includes its header, and records a
fatal log message as the abort message, only under __BIONIC__. A
device build against another C library that provides bionic's
android_set_abort_message defines __ANDROID__ but not __BIONIC__: the
aborter then calls an undeclared function and fatal messages never
reach a crash report. Treat __ANDROID__ like __BIONIC__ at these
guards. No change for Soong variants: device builds define both,
linux_bionic defines __BIONIC__.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no Soong variant defines __ANDROID__ without __BIONIC__]
Patch-Reason: the guards are compiled inside liblog, out of reach of the launcher, loader and environment; defining __BIONIC__ instead would change the libc++ ABI on glibc
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 liblog/logger_write.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/liblog/logger_write.cpp b/liblog/logger_write.cpp
index 3c6ccd0f67b73a98dde89fbad298e609fc04a725..4f596043795475c1f68b8c0aa8f9860b7957ba5e 100644
--- a/liblog/logger_write.cpp
+++ b/liblog/logger_write.cpp
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <sys/time.h>
 
-#ifdef __BIONIC__
+#if defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 #include <android/set_abort_message.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -373,7 +373,7 @@ void __android_log_write_log_message(__android_log_message* log_message) {
     log_message->tag = GetDefaultTag().c_str();
   }
 
-#if __BIONIC__
+#if defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
   if (log_message->priority == ANDROID_LOG_FATAL) {
     android_set_abort_message(log_message->message);
   }
